# =============================================================================
#  COMMODITIES SIGNAL DASHBOARD - Vol, VRP, Relative Value, Lead-Lag Monitor
#
#  IMPORTANT / EDUCATIONAL USE:
#  This dashboard produces systematic trade-idea candidates, not investment advice.
#  Every signal should be checked against liquidity, event risk, curve structure,
#  contract specs, options market depth, and desk risk limits before any trade.
#
# =============================================================================
#  WHAT WAS FIXED VS PRIOR VERSION
# =============================================================================
#
#  1) "Pairs / relative value" was too vague: fade or ride?
#     FIX:
#       - Correlation-break signals now produce an explicit rule-based action:
#           A) Corr breakdown vs normally related pair:
#              FADE dispersion = buy recent underperformer / sell recent outperformer.
#           B) Corr spike vs normally related pair:
#              RIDE regime = buy recent outperformer / sell recent underperformer.
#       - This is still only a heuristic. The code labels the action and the logic.
#
#  2) Lead-lag catch-up was barely showing.
#     FIX:
#       - The old filter required high average rolling correlation across the full
#         history and could suppress many pairs.
#       - Lead-lag now runs only on economically logical pairs, but with a cleaner
#         rolling-window test and a lower default minimum peak correlation.
#       - The trade is now explicit:
#             if leader outperformed recently -> BUY laggard
#             if leader underperformed recently -> SELL laggard
#
#  3) Softs were dominating vol trades.
#     FIX:
#       - Added manual vol-liquidity tiers.
#       - Added stale-IV detection.
#       - Added per-engine and per-asset-class caps so one market cluster cannot
#         dominate the feed.
#       - Added a "Min vol quality" control. Default excludes lowest quality vol
#         signals and stale IV.
#
#  4) Too many correlation breaks.
#     FIX:
#       - Correlation pairs are restricted to economically logical sets:
#           energy vs energy
#           metals vs metals
#           ags vs ags
#           livestock vs livestock
#           macro overlays vs everything
#       - Random unrelated pairs like Silver / Soybean Meal are no longer scanned.
#       - Added per-engine caps to keep the feed balanced.
#
#  5) How IV and realized vol work.
#     EXPLANATION:
#       - Realized vol here is historical volatility:
#             daily returns over RV_WINDOW days,
#             annualized by sqrt(252),
#             expressed in vol points / percent.
#       - Implied vol is market-implied future volatility embedded in option prices.
#         It is not "today's historical vol." It is the option market's forward-
#         looking volatility level for roughly the option tenor represented by the
#         Bloomberg field. Here we use bq.data.hist_put_imp_vol, understood as
#         roughly 30d ATM put implied volatility where available.
#       - IV > RV means the option market is pricing more future volatility than the
#         asset recently realized. That is the variance risk premium idea.
#
#  6) Why IV sometimes looks flat, e.g. Palladium.
#     EXPLANATION:
#       - Flat IV can happen because of sparse option quotes, stale marks, vendor
#         interpolation, exchange holidays, or low option liquidity.
#       - The code now flags "stale IV" when recent IV changes too little and excludes
#         stale vol signals by default.
#
#  7) Illiquid vol products might produce useless signals.
#     FIX:
#       - Added VOL_QUALITY tiers and stale-IV filters.
#       - Lower-quality products can still be viewed if the user chooses.
#
#  8) "Recompute no refresh" was unclear.
#     FIX:
#       - Renamed to "Apply controls".
#       - It re-runs the analytics using already downloaded/cached data.
#       - It does not call Bloomberg again.
#
#  9) Long straddle / gamma, short premium / spreads explanation.
#     EXPLANATION:
#       - Buy vol:
#           You buy options when IV looks cheap and you expect future realized vol
#           and/or implied vol to rise.
#           Long straddle = long call + long put, same strike/expiry.
#           Long gamma means the position benefits from large underlying moves and
#           can be dynamically hedged.
#           Other buy-vol expressions: long strangle, call/put, calendar, option
#           spread, variance swap if available.
#       - Sell vol:
#           You sell options when IV looks rich and you expect future realized vol
#           and/or implied vol to fall.
#           Short premium means collecting option premium.
#           Spreads define downside better than naked short options.
#           Other sell-vol expressions: short straddle/strangle, iron fly/condor,
#           credit spreads, variance swap short if available.
#
# 10) Correlation universe was too broad / illogical.
#     FIX:
#       - Added asset-class gating.
#       - Macro overlays still run vs everything.
#
# 11) Should IV today be compared to future realized vol?
#     EXPLANATION:
#       - For a live signal, the future realized volatility is unknown.
#       - The standard live VRP proxy compares today's IV with recent realized vol.
#       - For research/backtesting, you can compare today's IV with realized vol
#         over the next 21 trading days, but that would be look-ahead biased in a
#         live dashboard. This code avoids look-ahead.
#
# 12) Too many description words / emojis.
#     FIX:
#       - Removed emojis.
#       - Reduced tab/header descriptions.
#       - Button names made plain.
#
# =============================================================================

